### B.2 Hybrid PIML-DT Training Procedure

```
Algorithm 2: Offline Hybrid PIML-DT Training with Adaptive Loss Weighting
Input:  High-fidelity simulation snapshots Q_full = {q(x,t_i)}_{i=1}^M
        Converged RANS baseline fields Q_phys = {q_phys(x,t_i)}
        Wall temperature measurements T_wall_meas
        Sensor calibration telemetry Y_cal
Output: Trained residual network weights Θ_DT; POD residual basis Φ_res

PHASE 1 — BASELINE RANS ENSEMBLE:
  for each operating condition c in calibration matrix:
    q_phys^(c) ← converged_RANS_solve(geometry, c, SST_k_omega)
  Q_phys ← {q_phys^(c)}

PHASE 2 — RESIDUAL FIELD CONSTRUCTION:
  for i = 1 to M:
    r_i ← q_full(x,t_i) − q_phys(x,t_i)
  R = {r_i}_{i=1}^M

PHASE 3 — POD BASIS ON RESIDUAL FIELD:
  C_res ← (1/M) R R^T
  Φ_res, Λ_res ← eigendecompose(C_res)
  r_res ← min{r: Σ_{i=1}^r λ_i / Σ λ_i ≥ 0.999}
  Φ_res ← first r_res columns

PHASE 4 — RESIDUAL NETWORK TRAINING:
  Initialize residual net weights Θ by Xavier initialization
  Initialize adaptive weights w = {w_data, w_phys, w_BC, w_IC, w_N, w_r}
      = {1,1,1,1,1,1}
  Initialize Adam optimizer with lr = 10^{-3}, β_1=0.9, β_2=0.999
  r_max ← 0.35 · field_norm(Q_phys)    // per-field correction bound

  for epoch = 1 to N_epochs:
    Sample N_d data points from (Q_full, Q_phys) pairs
    Sample N_c collocation points from Ω × [0,T]
    Sample N_b boundary points from ∂Ω × [0,T]
    Sample N_i initial points from Ω × {0}
    Sample N_w wall points from ∂Ω_wall × [0,T]

    L_data ← compute_data_loss(Θ, data_points, Q_full, Q_phys)
    L_phys ← compute_physics_residual(Θ, collocation_points, Q_phys)
    L_BC   ← compute_BC_loss(Θ, boundary_points)
    L_IC   ← compute_IC_loss(Θ, initial_points)

    // Neumann heat flux loss
    q_meas ← inverse_heat_conduction(T_wall_meas, λ_T)
    L_Neumann ← compute_neumann_loss(Θ, wall_points, q_meas)

    // Residual magnitude regularization
    L_reg ← compute_residual_bound_loss(Θ, collocation_points, r_max)

    // Adaptive weight update (NTK-informed)
    g_data ← ||∇_Θ L_data||;    g_phys ← ||∇_Θ L_phys||
    g_BC   ← ||∇_Θ L_BC||;      g_IC   ← ||∇_Θ L_IC||
    g_N    ← ||∇_Θ L_Neumann||; g_r    ← ||∇_Θ L_reg||
    g_mean ← mean(g_data, g_phys, g_BC, g_IC, g_N, g_r)
    w_data ← g_mean/g_data;  w_phys ← g_mean/g_phys
    w_BC   ← g_mean/g_BC;    w_IC   ← g_mean/g_IC
    w_N    ← g_mean/g_N;     w_r    ← g_mean/g_r

    L_total ← w_data·L_data + w_phys·L_phys + w_BC·L_BC
             + w_IC·L_IC + w_N·L_Neumann + w_r·L_reg
    Θ ← Adam_update(Θ, ∇_Θ L_total)

    if epoch mod 1000 == 0:
      RMSE_state ← validate_state(Θ, Y_cal)
      RMSE_flux  ← validate_heat_flux(Θ, T_wall_meas)
      if RMSE_state < 0.05 and RMSE_flux < 0.10:
        break

  return Θ_DT ← Θ, Φ_res
```

